---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy · Week Without Driving Las Vegas';
const description = 'What lvwwd.org collects, how it is used, and how to ask for deletion.';
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <section class="container-page page-top reading">
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-on-surface-variant">Last updated September 29, 2026</p>

    <article class="prose-doc mt-8">
      <p>
        Las Vegans for Better Transit (LVBT) runs lvwwd.org. You can read the guides, find a bus,
        and play Bingo without signing up. My week and the giveaway require a sign-up and an
        internet connection.
      </p>

      <h2>What you give us</h2>
      <p>
        For the giveaway, we ask for your first name, email address, ZIP code, county, and whether
        you are 18 or older or 13 to 17. An Instagram handle is optional. We use these details to
        identify your entries, check eligibility, send a My week link when email delivery is
        available, and contact the winner.
      </p>
      <p>
        For a trip you enter in My week, we keep the date, travel mode, and description. You can
        separately tell us what was hard. A post link or screenshot is optional. For an Instagram
        tag logged by a volunteer, we keep the day and a post link if available. Volunteers use this
        information to review entries. LVBT may use what people report about travel barriers to
        advocate for better transit, stops, and sidewalks. We will ask before publishing a story or
        image that identifies you; checking the sharing box on an entry gives that permission for
        its post or screenshot.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you sign up through a partner link, we record that partner with your sign-up so LVBT can
        count sign-ups from its outreach. The site does not show your identity to partners. Bingo
        marks are saved in your browser; when you are signed in, your card can also be saved with
        your account so it follows you to another device.
      </p>

      <h2>Links, cookies, and notifications</h2>
      <p>
        My week uses a sign-in cookie on your device. A link sent to your email can sign in another
        device, so do not share it. Sign out to end the session on one device. Email links are sent
        through Resend when delivery is configured; if it is unavailable, this device can remain
        signed in.
      </p>
      <p>
        If browser reminders become available and you turn them on, we store the subscription
        address and keys your browser gives us, along with when you subscribed and the last day
        sent. Stop reminders in My week to remove that subscription.
      </p>

      <h2>Who handles the information</h2>
      <p>
        LVBT volunteers with access to the protected review page can see sign-ups and entries.
        Cloudflare hosts the site, stores campaign records and uploaded screenshots, and protects
        the forms. Resend handles sign-in emails when it is configured. A registered Instagram tag
        is reviewed by a volunteer on Instagram; Instagram handles that content under its own terms.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site does not currently load a separate analytics script. LVBT does not sell campaign
        information or send sign-up addresses to its newsletter. The newsletter link takes you to a
        separate sign-up run by LVBT.
      </p>

      <h2>Deletion and your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Campaign records, sign-in links, Bingo records tied to an account, draw records, and
        notification subscriptions are scheduled for deletion starting November 30, 2026. Uploaded
        screenshots may take additional daily cleanup runs. You can ask us to delete your
        information sooner at <a href="mailto:wwd@lasvegasfortransit.org"
          >wwd@lasvegasfortransit.org</a
        >. Deleting an entry removes it from the draw. You can also remove Bingo data saved only on
        your device through your browser's site storage settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions about your information? Email <a href="mailto:wwd@lasvegasfortransit.org"
          >wwd@lasvegasfortransit.org</a
        >.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
